After seven, eight years we see Mashallah this year's spring
is beautiful.

89
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Erê pir xweş e, elhemdulillah ji Xwedê re.
 
Yes it is very beautiful, praise be to God.

90
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Naha ev we kilîkê mêst berhev dikî, lê tu tiştên din tevî
dikî?
 
Now you are collecting yogurt kilik, but are you mixing
other things?

91
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Ez van tevî dikim, ez yekê jê dikim.
 
I mix these, I pick some.

92
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Kilîkên tivizîkan hene jê dikim.
 
There are tender kiliks, I pick them.

93
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Kilîkê teşkîl e. Zehterê haşîna yekê jê dikim.
 
It's mixed kilik. I pick some wild thyme.

94
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Teşkîle îşta.
 
Mix them like this.

95
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Maqsed zorat bi xwe pir xweş e.
 
The goal is for the crop to be very good itself.

96
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Gerek tevlîhev be ne?
 
It must be mixed, right?

97
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Ne, gerek tevlîhev be. Êdî wextê wê ye. Wextê zoratê ye
naha.
 
No, it needs to be mixed. It's its time now. It's crop time
now.

98
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Û hinek jî hene Xaltîka Rengîn bes kilîkê mêst bi tenê
dikelînin.
 
And there are some, Aunt Rengin, who only boil yogurt kilik.

99
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Erê feyda xwe heye hinek jî dikin leçer.
 
Yes, it has its benefits, some also make lecher.

100
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Dikin leçer.
 
They make lecher.

101
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Avê wê jê dikin, tê de qelî dikin, dikin leçer.
 
They drain its water, fry it in there, they make lecher.

102
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Bêhna wê çiqas xweş e.
 
Its smell is so nice.

103
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Erê welle bêhna wê pir xweş e.
 
Yes, by God, its smell is very nice.

104
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Hê dema tu jê dikî, naha tu diçî dikelînî.
 
Even as you pick it, now you will go and boil it.

105
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Ev anqîrê we ye?
 
Is this your land?

106
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Ev anqîrê me ye.
 
This is our land.

107
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

108
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Naha hewşê me ye, malê me ye.
 
Now it's our courtyard, our house.

109
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Rind e, elhemdulillah. Pezê me heye?
 
It's good, praise be to God. Do we have sheep?

110
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Pezê me heye.
 
We have sheep.

111
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Naha wextê şîrmestê jî ye he?
 
Now is the milking time too, right?

112
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Erê naha wextê şîrmestê ye, naha me penîrê xwe çêkir, naha
hatim biçkê kilîkan berhev dikim.
 
Yes, now is the milking time, now we made our cheese, now I
came to collect some kilik.

113
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Te rind kiriye welle. Xwedê sihetê xweş bide we.
 
You did well, by God. May God give you good health.

114
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Welle em ji Efrînê aciz dibin, min got ez herim gundê
Sêviya.
 
By God, we get bored of Afrin, I said let me go to the
village of Seviya.

115
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Bavê min ê bi rehmê, tim dihat virê.
 
My late father used to come here all the time.

116
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Bi bîra bavê xwe min tê vî gundî.
 
The memory of my father brings me to this village.

117
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Bi rastî ez cem Apê Henan ez diçim. Ez ê herim wî bibînim.
 
Actually I am going to Uncle Henan. I will go see him.

118
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Ehlen û sehlen.
 
Welcome.

119
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Bavê te bi rehmê tiştekî ... bêhna bavê min lê tê.
 
Your late father was something... he reminds me of my
father.

120
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Hesyaya wî, çêbûna wî, dîtina wî li vir e, ez ji bo wê diçim
cem Apê Henan.
 
His feelings, his being, his presence is here, that is why I
am going to Uncle Henan.

121
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Bavê we bi hev re esker bûn, wî çaxî bi hev re bûn.
 
Your fathers were soldiers together, they were together back
then.

122
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Em diçûn... saetên dirêj em bi hev re bûn.
 
We used to go... we spent long hours together.

123
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Rind e, seheta we xweş be.
 
That is nice, may you have good health.

124
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Tu jî rind e.
 
You are good too.

125
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Em aciz dibin em diçin Sêviya.
 
We get bored so we go to Seviya.

126
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Welle, baş e hûn hatin Sêviya.
 
By God, it is good that you came to Seviya.

127
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Baş e, seheta we xweş be.
 
Good, may you have good health.

128
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Seheta te jî xweş be, welle baş e.
 
May you have good health too, by God, it's good.

129
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Em tu naxweşiyan nabînin, em tim bi xêr û xweşiyê da bin.
 
May we see no illnesses, may we always be in goodness and
health.

130
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Em giş bi hev re yek bin, yekbûn baş e.
 
May we all be united, unity is good.

131
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Tiştek wek yekbûn heye.
 
There is a thing such as unity.

132
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Maşallah pir e jî.
 
Mashallah, there is a lot of it too.

133
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Ne pir e, çiqas tu dixwazî tu jê dikî.
 
It's not a lot, you pick as much as you want.

134
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Belê temaşevanên me yê hêja naha jî em ligel Kakê Cemîl û
Kakê Azad.
 
Yes, our dear viewers, now we are with Brother Cemil and
Brother Azad.

135
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

136
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Ev meşleh, ev ne berê bav û kalên me çêdikirin ser xwe...
 
This meshleh (cloak), didn't our forefathers make this to
wear...

137
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Erê her şivanekî me ev meşlehên wiha li vir e, me li gund
dît...
 
Yes, every shepherd of ours has these meshlehs here, we saw
it in the village...

138
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Me merheba dikir, dihatin...
 
We used to greet them, they used to come...

139
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
U çûkê jî hebû. Le çûk wergiya...
 
And there were birds too. But the birds...

140
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Lê çûk tiştekî nabe ...
 
But nothing happens to the birds...

141
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Em bi cûreyekî dîtir karê xwe dikin ... şivanên xwe weha
dikin.
 
We do our work in another way... our shepherds do it like
this.

142
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Lê berê daha xweş bû.
 
But it was better before.

143
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Kakê Azad berê ev dema ku li derve dihatin dewar dikirin,
zivistanê, berf û baran dihat, xwe bi wî meşlehî digirt, ne
berf, ne tiştek diçû wî.
 
Brother Azad, before when they came outside to graze the
cattle in the winter, when it rained and snowed, they
covered themselves with this meshleh, neither snow nor
anything got to them.

144
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Ne welle tu tişt nediçû.
 
No, by God, nothing got to them.

145
