Nîsan e. Naha î xelk disekinin, da be ez key munê çêkim
wextî firêza? Na! Wextî firêza, çû wiya şîr e. Na? Tebîeta
xwe avêt, bes hema rewş ê rûyê her tiştkî gîl û çîçekan e.
Ji xêra Nîsanê ye.
 
All of that is medicine. All of it comes from this blessing
and abundance of the earth. In April. Now people wait,
saying "Let me make my provisions during the harvest time?"
No! During the harvest time, how is the milk? No? It lost
its nature, but the essence of everything is from the
flowers and blossoms. It's from the blessing of April.

448
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:08,000
Her tişt. Her tiştkî xweş û şêrîn û fîtamîn têda heye, meha
Nîsanê. Heta berxê miyan e, di nêçê xwe salek bilke nav
wexta da sade...
 
Everything. Everything pleasant and sweet and full of
vitamins is in it, the month of April. Even the lambs of the
ewes, they thrive in a year, maybe in that time it's
simple...

449
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:14,000
Nav pez danin, şîrê nîsanê dixwin. Maşallah bex! Dîsa
nexweşî. Nedlînin eva ewe ewe...
 
Put them among the sheep, they drink April's milk. Mashallah
the lamb! Again, sickness. They don't show that... that is
that is...

450
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:17,000
Helî e sal temam e, sal dewre qe zirar naket.
 
Yes the year is complete, the sheep do not face any loss
during the year.

451
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:35,000
Bixwudê qe ze çike dewr lêket. Nexweşî ket nava dewr e lê
am, meselan li Sûrîyê giştik e. Nexweşî yek te wekê vêra
digotin. Dibên qulaî ye. We yekî çike zirar go da me, berxî
çîçik dimirin. Erê welle ey, me derman dikirin, me mualece
dikir. Elhemdulillah Xudê razî.
 
By God, whatever happened happened to the sheep. A disease
hit the sheep but we, for example, everywhere in Syria. A
sickness hit, here they called it "Qulai" (Foot-and-Mouth
Disease). That caused some damage to us, the little lambs
died. Yes by God, hey, we gave them medicine, we treated
them. Praise be to God, may God bless.

452
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:38,000
Xwedê rizqê we bişênî ke Kakê. Em pir kêfxweş bûn, bi dîtina
we.
 
May God bless your sustenance, Kak. We were very happy to
see you.

453
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:39,000
Ser çavan.
 
On my eyes.

454
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:40,000
Rûyê te.
 
On your face.

455
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Sax bî. Ser çavê me. Sax bî. Ser çavê min.
 
Be healthy. On our eyes. Be healthy. On my eyes.

456
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:47,000
Ehlen û sehlen. Çi emrî te heye? Çi gotinek te heye? Te
dixwestê tiştî kevin...
 
Welcome. Do you have any orders? Do you have any words? You
wanted old things...

457
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:51,000
Kak Xelîl, ez spasî te dikim. Em tiştê kevin bi bîra wan
miletî dikin. Ser çava, ez hazir im.
 
Kak Xelil, I thank you. We remind the people of old things.
Upon my eyes, I am ready.

458
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:52,000
Destên te sax bin.
 
Bless your hands.

459
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:57,000
Belê temeşevanên hêja, em nakin eslê xwe bîr bikin. Kakê
Reşîd, me çawa dewr diqesand?
 
Yes dear viewers, we do not forget our origins. Kak Reshid,
how did we shear the sheep?

460
00:35:57,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Erê. Xudê rehma xwe li tirbê bab û fîkê te ke. Bîra xwe te
anî bîr? Dinya da...
 
Yes. May God have mercy on the graves of your father and
ancestors. Did you remember? In this world...

461
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Maşallah. Maşallah. Maşallah. Jimer gotî, ji romkê. Ji ber
ku ti eyar nakî bin bar ne?
 
Mashallah. Mashallah. Mashallah. You said, from the Roman
times. Because you don't keep them under the rain, right?

462
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:09,000
Welle, we nakê, kak Xelîl as bîra te ne kirî kake Xelîl.
 
By God, they don't, Kak Xelil, I didn't remind you, Kak
Xelil.

463
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:11,000
Mere aslî xwe bîr de ke...
 
One should not forget their origins...

464
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:18,000
Ne welle, Xwedê rehma xwe li baba û fîkê te ke, ya reb, di
vê dinyayê de, çi rind e. Gerek însan e, gîş kerdî eslî xwe
bîr nakin.
 
No, by God, may God have mercy on your father and ancestors,
oh Lord, in this world, how beautiful it is. People must, no
one should ever forget their origins.

465
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:20,000
Na'em. Wêne ye...
 
Yes. That's true...

466
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Gerek tim hînbîr xweta wa tişkê. Sehet a te xweş. Û înşallah
bi lez ez bêjim, em niha, rûkî em bav û kalê me. Divê însan
mezinê xwe ti zata ne...
 
One must always remember such things. Bless your health. And
God willing, I'll say quickly, we now, are the descendants
of our fathers and grandfathers. People must know their
elders...

467
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:32,000
Ne... gerek mera bêje... te bîr nakirî?
 
No... one should say... didn't you forget?

468
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:40,000
Ne, te bîr nakirî? te bîr... Seya te xweş. Ê, deşt erê, ez
jê xwe wene deqesînim kak Xelîl, aştê te...
 
No, didn't you forget? didn't you... Bless your health. Yes,
well, I shear like that, Kak Xelil, your peace...

469
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:43,000
Bes înşalle roj bi roj e jê dibe Kakê Reşîd.
 
But God willing, day by day it will pass, Kak Reshid.

470
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:49,000
Sîhhat a te xweş. Înşallah, kêm anî çênabin. Tiştê ger
mazinên me ji bavê, bihale me. Ji mezinên xwe, ji opelên
xwe.
 
Bless your health. God willing, there won't be any
shortcomings. Things that our elders left to us. From our
elders, from our ancestors.

471
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Maşallah, maşallah. Kakê Xelîl welle ti rûmî xelas kirî.
Welle Kak Reşîd, me bîr ne kirî ye.
 
Mashallah, mashallah. Kak Xelil, by God you finished the
Romans. By God, Kak Reshid, we haven't forgotten.

472
00:36:56,000 --> 00:37:00,000
Lî no a peze, me gîha ye... em e nisan in em e gundî mal
zemin...
 
Well now, this sheep, it reached us... we are people, we are
villagers, landlords...

473
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:08,000
Ne hûn ci kakê. Camêr, te hûrbîn te ma go hetta pezê berê?
Şivanê berê heybeta xwe hebû. Gşk van de dihan dengê zengil
e kî. Litolikan deko bi vêsnê non. Veno dergeh ...
 
What are you talking about, brother? Gentleman, didn't you
look closely, didn't you say even the sheep of the past? The
shepherd of the past had his dignity. They all brought the
sound of a bell. With leggings, they would wear them. Then
the gate...

474
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:11,000
Warto we bage... Destên te sax bin, kak Xelîl, Xwedê ji te
razî be kak.
 
Here's the bag... Bless your hands, Kak Xelil, may God be
pleased with you, brother.

475
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:27,000
Seta te pir xweş...
 
Bless your health so much...

476
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:37,000
(Instrumental music and wordless vocals)
 
(Instrumental music and wordless vocals)

477
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Sibeh bixêr, keca delalê.
 
Good morning, beautiful girl.

478
00:37:42,000 --> 00:38:00,000
Bxunavê çavan kil kir. Xelazek av çiqinek nan, muje û
bastêqan hazir kir. Lehespê taf mistî war be... Emî da min,
min ax kel kir. Çayek kurmancî lê bipirse, her gundekî ser
...
 
She wiped the dew from her eyes. She prepared a drop of
water, a morsel of bread, raisins, and dried fruit pulp. On
the swift horse, be brave... Come to me, I have boiled the
earth. Ask for a Kurdish tea, in every village...

479
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:20,000
Em atêşdarên axê ne, derî bi derî difitilin de vanan e. Em
atêşdarên axê ne, derî bi derî difitilin de vanan e.
 
We are the fire-keepers of the earth, we wander door to door
for these things. We are the fire-keepers of the earth, we
wander door to door for these things.

480
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:31,000
Hec Xelîlî ku kek Can e da.. Cindirê sêvê Rihayê da. Derdê
Hesendê lankê da. Kenî lê veye ya xweda.
 
Hec Xelil who gave it to brother Can... In the ragged apple
of Urfa. The sorrow of Hesende in the cradle. Laughter came
to her, oh God.

481
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:41,000
Hec Xelîlî ku kek Can e da.. Cindirê sêvê Rihayê da. Derdê
Hesendê lankê da. Kenî lê veye ya xweda.
 
Hec Xelil who gave it to brother Can... In the ragged apple
of Urfa. The sorrow of Hesende in the cradle. Laughter came
to her, oh God.

482
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:50,000
Kaniyek heye pir çemê da ne. Xizên bi sîr fan û xersan...
def û sirne dengê çokan, bi hesiya xwaze xwazan e.
 
There is a spring in many rivers. The poor with garlic, fans
and bears... the drum and zurna, the sound of knees, it was
felt by the suitors.

483
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:52,000
Xelîl dibêjin, berê da we dibêjin...
 
Xelil they say, they used to say in the past...

484
00:38:52,000 --> 00:39:00,000
Mî, te ji gur di bîrê daye. Gur jî ji bîr nekî. Kîço gur ji
bîr dikî. Doxê kit bibin hev ringe.
 
You have reminded the ewe of the wolf. Don't forget the wolf
either. How could you forget the wolf. They will be gathered
together.

485
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:14,000
Heke war e qese de gûr jî bîr meke ve. Me ti qet mihi di nav
ringe da gûr ji bîr dikin. Em yek xe nale ve derê daxin em
di bîn gûr jî ma ke, da here gûr jî me ke. Bes doxî kat bi
naberinga, gûr bi bîr te kê.
 
If it's a story, don't forget the wolf. We never forget the
wolf when the sheep are in the pen. We bring a cry here, we
say don't let the wolf come, let him go, don't let the wolf
come. Just let them get into the pen, the wolf will
remember.

486
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:16,000
Xwedê rizqê we mehafize bike kakê Reşîd.
 
May God protect your sustenance, Kak Reshid.

487
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:21,000
Ti sax bî kakê Xelîl. Em pir keyfxweş min we roja xwe dî bi
te. Te rojek aferîn, bi me de derbas kir.
 
May you be well, Kak Xelil. We are very happy we saw you
today. You spent a wonderful day with us.

488
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:22,000
Sahet a te xweş.
 
Bless your health.

489
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:31,000
Tu sax bî kak Xelîl ez pirs dikim e... Oh berî çi qasî te
bîra me, em pir keyfxweş bîn gundê Sêwiya. Her car we rûnî,
em hey wan de de me kî... de rastî. Em derbas bûn, û me
silavêk ji te wa...
 
May you be well, Kak Xelil, I ask... Oh, how long you've
remembered us, we were very happy in the village of Seviya.
Every time you sat down, we were always with them...
honestly. We passed by, and we send you a greeting...

490
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Em di gazincê, yanî em bihêvîne e, bi gotina de wahane. Şûre
de wahan e, e di xazin ji ve qenale çi çikê em gi lî kî lafê
miletê ze qne am debazê ceb dibên, em de gazin ce e şeku ye
ê gûtina van e de biken.
 
We are complaining, I mean we are hoping, they were saying
it like this. The sword was like this, we want from this
channel what we say in the words of the people, they
complain... we go to the pocket, we say, we complain about
what shape their words take.

491
00:39:42,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Bixudê, xwedê şeka na di ke. Elhemdulillah em bes dixwazin î
la nav we milletî bigerin, ev tiştî me i kevin, bi bîr tînin
e va ci lî me yi axer, zanibe em çi afirênerine. Afirêneriya
xwe, ji bîr nekin kese li der wa am pir dixwazin zarokê
wa... tabî mîhtîrame ye ji war a.
 
By God, God does not make doubt. Praise be to God, we only
want to wander among the people, to remember our old things,
so our younger generation knows what creators we are. Our
creations, let no one outside forget them, we really want
their children... of course we have respect for them.

492
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:02,000
Zarok ê piçûk ew an ha qesem bi Xwedê tiştî dibînin.
 
These young children, I swear to God, they see things.

